WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.020
This video was made possible by Skillshare.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:08.639
Learn from over 25,000 classes for free for
two months at skl.sh/wendover6.

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:15.639
No sports league in the world makes more money
than the American National Football League.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:20.020
The NFL earns more yearly revenue than the
English Premier League, the Champions League,

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.000
Formula One, the Japanese Nippon Professional
Baseball League, and the Kontinental Hockey

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.640
League combined.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:30.160
It is by far the largest sports league in
the world by revenue.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.030
Making up the NFL are 32 football teams each
themselves essentially acting as their own

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.690
distinct businesses.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.320
These teams are spread out all across the
contiguous United States—some only 30 miles

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:47.440
or 45 kilometers apart from each other, some
nearly 3,000 miles or 4,500 kilometers apart.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.399
Now, American football teams are some of the
largest in sports, both physically and in

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:53.399
numbers.

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:58.239
They have a roster of 56 players—the majority
of which play in any given game.

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:03.010
These players weigh on average about 250 pounds
or 110 kilograms.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:06.580
This team size leads to some particular travel
needs.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.450
Players each require a first class seat or,
at the very least, the seat next to them free

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:15.750
in economy meaning those 56 players take up
far more than 56 seats.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.350
On top of that, a team typically brings more
than 100 support staff and an immense amount

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.960
of cargo to each away game.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.390
With the exception of the largest, most valuable
ones, most other professional sports teams

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:33.619
in the US will just fly on chartered narrow-body
aircraft like a320’s, 737’s, or 757’s,

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:39.430
but most NFL teams, given their size, require
something larger.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:44.200
NFL teams tend to charter their aircraft from
commercial airlines—American, Delta, United,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:48.189
or Hawaiian Airlines—and they’ll typically
fly something a bit larger than other teams

00:01:48.189 --> 00:01:53.500
like a 767 or sometimes even a 777, but the
nature of this charter job makes finding a

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.670
plane to take them particularly difficult.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.640
You see, let’s take the example of the New
York Jets’ last game of the 2018 season

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.920
versus the New England Patriots on December
30th.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:10.479
For this game, they left the day before on
a United Airlines 767-400 at 3:37 pm landing

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:14.450
30 minutes later, at 4:07 pm, in Providence,
Rhode Island.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:19.640
The plane then sat on the ground at Providence
airport for the next 26 hours until the game

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.640
was over.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.700
The following day, the plane took off at 6:30
pm bound for New York.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.980
The aircraft’s previous flight had been
to Buenos Aires and its next flight was to

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:33.230
London and yet for these 26 hours, United
only made money from the half hour charter

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.260
flight to and from Providence.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:39.720
It’s easy to understand why this wouldn’t
really be worth it to the airline, but at

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.140
least the Jets are located next to a United
Airlines hub at Newark airport.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:48.500
Many teams, like the New Orleans Saints, for
example, are not located in a city with any

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.840
airline hub.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.730
That makes finding an airline to take their
charter contract even more difficult.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.319
That’s because, for example, when the team
had to travel to Charlotte last season, the

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:03.069
767 that took them had to fly in empty from
Houston, the nearest United hub, then fly

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:08.100
to Charlotte, sit on the ground for 33 hours,
fly back to New Orleans, then once again fly

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.970
empty—this time all the way to New York.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:15.530
All told, for the 2 hours and 51 minutes of
flight time United was paid for, they used

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:18.860
this airplane for about 44 hours.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:23.209
Being located away from an airline hub, where
planes are based, means charter flights will

00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:27.010
almost always require a plane flying in empty.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:31.650
It is for this reason that airlines are raising
rates or just flat-out stopping flying NFL

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:36.540
teams as they find normal, commercial flying
a more lucrative use of their aircraft.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.540
American Airlines, in recent years, for example,
dropped all the many teams they previously

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.569
flew except for the Carolina Falcons, the
Dallas Cowboys, and the Philadelphia Eagles—three

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:47.959
teams located at their hub airports.

00:03:47.959 --> 00:03:52.269
More teams have moved their contract to dedicated
charter companies such as Atlas Air or Miami

00:03:52.269 --> 00:03:57.159
Air International, while the New England Patriots
even bought their own set of planes to solve

00:03:57.159 --> 00:03:58.489
this issue.

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:01.849
Some other teams still have contracts with
commercial airlines but have switched to flying

00:04:01.849 --> 00:04:05.350
multiple smaller planes as these can be in
less demand.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:10.660
The Indianapolis Colts, for example, now typically
travel in two Delta 757’s leaving within

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.549
a half hour of each other.

00:04:12.549 --> 00:04:16.780
Other American sports, such as Hockey, Baseball,
and Basketball, don’t have nearly as much

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:21.319
of a problem because they play far more games
a season, which makes their contract a more

00:04:21.319 --> 00:04:25.699
attractive one to the airlines, and they also
typically use smaller aircraft of which there

00:04:25.699 --> 00:04:27.289
are more available.

00:04:27.289 --> 00:04:31.210
The NFL briefly considered investing in its
own fleet of aircraft or at least negotiating

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:36.210
a deal with an airline in bulk, like the NBA
does with Delta, but for now, NFL teams are

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:41.139
seeing their travel costs skyrocket as the
laws of supply and demand take hold.

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:44.870
After losing their contract with American
Airlines, for example, the Jacksonville Jaguars

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:50.369
saw their travel costs double to $4 million
a year as they chartered an Atlas Air 747

00:04:50.369 --> 00:04:56.309
and remember, those $4 million pay for the
travel costs to a mere eight away games.

00:04:56.309 --> 00:05:00.849
But the NFL’s most daunting logistics problem
is not this.

00:05:00.849 --> 00:05:05.830
Their most daunting logistics problem relates
to the NFL’s other big problem—expansion.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:11.090
You see, part of the reason the NFL is the
most valuable sports league in the world is

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:15.089
because of how saturated the football market
is in the US.

00:05:15.089 --> 00:05:18.979
57% of Americans identify as NFL fans.

00:05:18.979 --> 00:05:23.969
That’s an amazing level of market saturation
for what is, at its core, a business, but

00:05:23.969 --> 00:05:28.979
that also presents a problem because, with
such a high proportion of the population already

00:05:28.979 --> 00:05:33.990
fans, it’s quite difficult for the NFL to
expand their audience, at least within the

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:34.990
US.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:39.380
In the past decade or so, the league has turned
its attention internationally.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:44.279
The NFL now plays regular season games in
Mexico City and London.

00:05:44.279 --> 00:05:49.669
These cities don’t have home teams but rather,
two teams from the US will come out and play.

00:05:49.669 --> 00:05:53.550
For the most part, these international games
are about promoting the sport in these two

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:57.599
countries which already have significant fanbases
watching the sport on TV.

00:05:57.599 --> 00:06:02.089
There’s never been more than one game a
season in Mexico City but in London, in the

00:06:02.089 --> 00:06:06.319
2019 season, they’re playing four regular
season games.

00:06:06.319 --> 00:06:11.050
With the 16 regular-season games per team
per year, any other city that has a resident

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:16.479
NFL team typically only has eight home games
meaning London’s quantity is really not

00:06:16.479 --> 00:06:17.809
that far off.

00:06:17.809 --> 00:06:22.719
What’s more, the Jacksonville Jaguars are
designated as a sort of home team for London

00:06:22.719 --> 00:06:26.599
and therefore play at least one of their games
there each year in an attempt to give the

00:06:26.599 --> 00:06:29.139
city and country a clear team to root for.

00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:33.319
The league has even said that it plans to
eventually have a full eight games per season

00:06:33.319 --> 00:06:37.009
in London—the same as any home city in the
US.

00:06:37.009 --> 00:06:41.449
The reason there are now so many NFL games
in London is because the sport of American

00:06:41.449 --> 00:06:45.590
football has gained significant inroads in
the UK audience.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:51.259
The NFL estimates that it has 13 million fans
in the UK, 4 million of which watch regularly,

00:06:51.259 --> 00:06:56.029
and 47,000 of which buy games to every single
NFL game in the UK.

00:06:56.029 --> 00:07:01.990
Its dedication to the UK has become so significant
that it contributed $12.5 million to the construction

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:05.050
of the new Tottenham Hotspur Stadium in north
London.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:09.469
This recently opened stadium was built to
become the home of the NFL in the UK.

00:07:09.469 --> 00:07:14.129
It has a permanent synthetic American football
pitch under its grass soccer field; purpose

00:07:14.129 --> 00:07:19.499
built, NFL-sized locker rooms; and a media
suite built to the preferences of NFL press.

00:07:19.499 --> 00:07:24.819
In the coming years, at least two NFL games
will occur each year at this stadium.

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:29.629
Now, the logistics of these international
games in London are formidable.

00:07:29.629 --> 00:07:35.120
When the Seahawks played in London in 2018,
they had to ship 1,150 rolls of athletic tape,

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:41.830
about 4,000 pounds or 1,800 kilograms of medical
supplies, 350 power adapters, 500 shoes, 240

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:47.009
pairs of socks, and tens of thousands of other
pounds of equipment to the city weeks ahead

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:48.319
of their arrival.

00:07:48.319 --> 00:07:52.300
Months before, they had to arrange for many
of their players, who had never left the US,

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.699
to get passports.

00:07:53.699 --> 00:07:57.099
The team’s trainers had to carefully schedule
their players sleep in the week leading up

00:07:57.099 --> 00:07:58.099
to reduce jet-lag.

00:07:58.099 --> 00:08:02.649
There’s even a hotel in Watford with a purpose
built American football practice pitch that

00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:03.789
the teams typically stay in.

00:08:03.789 --> 00:08:09.089
While these London matches come at great difficulty
and force teams to sacrifice a coveted home

00:08:09.089 --> 00:08:13.689
game, the teams and their owners seem to tolerate
them given their infrequency and the promise

00:08:13.689 --> 00:08:15.099
of the UK market.

00:08:15.099 --> 00:08:19.860
But the promise of the UK market could push
the NFL to stretch beyond eight international

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.539
series games a year there.

00:08:21.539 --> 00:08:26.610
You see, there is some very real, very serious
discussion of putting a National Football

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.639
League team in London.

00:08:28.639 --> 00:08:33.279
There is little doubt that the city and country
could support a team in terms of fanbase.

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:38.060
The issue, according to the league’s commissioner,
would be having one solitary team stationed

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:42.149
more than 3,000 miles or 5,000 kilometers
away from the next.

00:08:42.149 --> 00:08:47.259
It would be an immense logistics problem considering
that, for the weekly games, teams would have

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:52.019
to take flights as long as eleven hours crossing
up to eight timezones.

00:08:52.019 --> 00:08:56.250
On the flip side, this London NFL team would
have to travel continuously throughout the

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:00.589
US for weeks at a time since, practically,
it wouldn’t make sense for them to return

00:09:00.589 --> 00:09:02.879
to London between the weekly games.

00:09:02.879 --> 00:09:06.769
This would come at enormous expense, would
likely impact their performance, and prove

00:09:06.769 --> 00:09:08.440
unpopular with their players.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:14.069
In addition, as the UK does not yet have significant
American football talent, the majority of

00:09:14.069 --> 00:09:18.480
this teams players would come from the US
and would need to be persuaded, either monetarily

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:21.610
or otherwise, to live outside their home country.

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:24.300
Those are just some of the cost problems.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:30.449
Beyond that, it is not cheap to fly a whole
NFL team over the Atlantic every week.

00:09:30.449 --> 00:09:34.759
For the international series games, teams
were flown on chartered Virgin Atlantic 747

00:09:34.759 --> 00:09:39.699
or a330’s arranged by the league, but if
London had a fully fledged NFL team, it would

00:09:39.699 --> 00:09:44.370
likely be treated just like any other team
meaning both them and their American competitors

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.810
would have to arrange their own flights.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.629
The wide-body planes teams would have to charter
to cross the Atlantic come at a cost of up

00:09:50.629 --> 00:09:52.850
to $50,000 per flight hour.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:57.110
That means that transatlantic travel costs,
just in terms of the flight, would be anywhere

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:03.629
between $650,000 for an east coast team or
up to a full $1 million for west coast teams.

00:10:03.629 --> 00:10:07.649
Teams also tend to carry tens of thousands
of pounds of cargo to each away game which

00:10:07.649 --> 00:10:09.470
would further escalate the cost.

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:13.960
While such an expense would be little issue
for large, wealthy teams like the Dallas Cowboys

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:18.150
or New England Patriots, teams with smaller
budgets like the Detroit Lions or Cleveland

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:22.449
Browns would certainly have more of an issue
with potentially adding an extra million in

00:10:22.449 --> 00:10:23.449
travel costs.

00:10:23.449 --> 00:10:28.019
But this level of team isolation is not unprecedented.

00:10:28.019 --> 00:10:32.389
Further west, in the middle of the Pacific,
the University of Hawaii has a division one

00:10:32.389 --> 00:10:36.019
college football team—the Hawaii Rainbow
Warriors.

00:10:36.019 --> 00:10:42.019
The closest team in their conference is 2,600
miles or 4,200 kilometers away in San Diego.

00:10:42.019 --> 00:10:44.540
To get there, they take a five hour flight.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:49.120
That’s only an hour or two faster than it
would take a London NFL team to get to its

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.350
closest competitor—the New England Patriots.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:55.990
While the furthest team in the Rainbow Warrior’s
conference is only a seven or eight hour flight

00:10:55.990 --> 00:11:00.700
away in Colorado Springs, Colorado, they do
play a number of non-conference games each

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:05.220
year which take them all the way to the US
east coast—an up to 10 hour flight away

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:09.759
from Honolulu which is almost exactly the
same as the longest required travel time for

00:11:09.759 --> 00:11:11.329
an NFL team to London.

00:11:11.329 --> 00:11:15.930
Not only that, but the Hawaii Rainbow Warriors
also have to balance their time with class

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:19.790
schedules which means that they travel to
their away games far closer to kickoff than

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:22.240
NFL teams typically do to London.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:26.470
The Rainbow Warriors regularly rack up more
travel miles than any professional football

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:27.470
team.

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:31.870
For example, in one particularly grueling
month in 2016, the team started its season

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:36.160
with an international match in Sydney, Australia,
then the next weekend played in Ann Arbor,

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:41.660
Michigan, then the weekend after that played
in Tucson, Arizona meaning they flew 25,000

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:45.420
miles or 40,000 kilometers in just one month.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:50.050
The Rainbow Warriors also make most of their
trips on commercial flights making their travel

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:52.839
even more difficult than that of NFL teams.

00:11:52.839 --> 00:11:57.120
Now, this does potentially give the team a
more significant home-field advantage since

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:00.440
they’re used to playing with jet lag while
their opponents, when they fly to Hawaii,

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:04.940
would not be, but it also supports the view
that, logistically, it would be possible to

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.920
add an NFL team in London.

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:11.370
There are even professional sports leagues
that already regularly require travel over

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.629
similar or greater distances.

00:12:13.629 --> 00:12:18.140
The Kontinental Hockey League, for example,
has teams spread out all across Asia and Eastern

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:22.649
Europe meaning the teams from Beijing, Vladivostok,
Khabarovsk, and Beijing regularly have to

00:12:22.649 --> 00:12:29.691
travel more than 4,000 miles or 6,500 kilometers
to play the teams from Minsk, Riga, and Helsinki.

00:12:29.691 --> 00:12:34.550
An even more extreme example would be Super
Rugby which has teams spread out across Japan,

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:37.949
Argentina, South Africa, Australia, and New
Zealand.

00:12:37.949 --> 00:12:42.149
With this, when the Tokyo Sunwolves play the
Buenos Aires Janguares, for example, they

00:12:42.149 --> 00:12:49.290
have to travel more than 11,000 miles or 18,000
kilometers each way to their match.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:54.139
Part of the NFL’s problem is just the pure
scale of their competitions with many tens

00:12:54.139 --> 00:12:58.880
of thousands of pounds of equipment and many
hundreds of staff traveling to each game.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:03.350
The problems are surmountable, though, at
a cost but this cost would be partially burdened

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:05.740
by every other team in the league.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:10.259
The question is then, given the promise of
adding a whole new country to the league,

00:13:10.259 --> 00:13:12.100
is the cost worth it.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:16.889
Now, if the NFL expands to London, one of
the first things the new team will need is

00:13:16.889 --> 00:13:17.889
a logo.

00:13:17.889 --> 00:13:21.300
Luckily, there’s a class on Skillshare for
that.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:25.459
Professional animator Fraser Davidson, who
actually has done design work for the NFL,

00:13:25.459 --> 00:13:28.800
teaches this fantastic course which walks
you through the process of creating your own

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:29.800
mascot.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:34.589
This is just one of over 25,000 classes on
Skillshare which each teach you something

00:13:34.589 --> 00:13:38.000
that you can use for your job, for school,
or just for fun.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:43.360
A few more that I would recommend are Storytelling
101, the Productivity Masterclass, and Cinematography

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:48.120
Basics, all of which you can download offline
on the iOS or Android apps.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:53.019
You can learn from any of these more than
25,000 classes for free for a month by signing

00:13:53.019 --> 00:13:58.089
up at skl.sh/wendover6 and you’ll be supporting
the show while you’re at it.

